{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119439","id":3677856479,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7bN6Lf","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119439","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119439.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119439.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119439","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119439/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119439/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119439/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/fec858e3b4fe38248aefe044632994f0c42badb8","number":119439,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix `PopupMenu` submenu positioning not accounting for margins","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #119386\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis fixes the issue of `PopupMenu` submenus not positioning the first item in the submenu aligned with the first item in the parent `PopupMenu`, by simply subtracting `get_margin(SIDE_TOP)` from the Y position.\r\n\r\nI also added subtraction of the search bar height and separation, similar to how it's done in `PopupMenu::_get_contents_minimum_size`, although I'm not sure if that's even a thing you'd want in submenus.\r\n\r\nI also threw in some slight refactoring, whereby the changes to `submenu_pos.y` is now split out from the `if (is_layout_rtl())` cases and dealt with separately, since there was no real need for that to happen there, and just resulted in duplicated code.\r\n\r\nLastly, I changed the calculation of the autohide top rect to share the same `item_top_y` offset as the submenu positioning, which also happens to fix a bug where the autohide region wasn't taking the search bar into account correctly, causing the submenu to flicker/re-open when moving between the parent item and submenu item.\r\n\r\n---\r\n_Disclaimer: AI tooling was used to help triage this, as well as make some minor edits. Any code not physically typed out by myself has been reviewed to the best of my ability._","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1332303119,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzMyMzAzMTE5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/regression","name":"regression","description":"","color":"ff63ac","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godote